# Folds romans-1-romans1-18-32.html (main) and romans-1-romasn1-reviewpic.html (Review, Weeks 1 & 2, last as the Recap).

=== Romans 1:18-32
--- Romans 1:18-32: The Logical Descent to Judgment [title]
overline: A study in Romans 1
heading: Romans 1:18-32: The Logical Descent to Judgment
sub: Paul’s argument uses a strict cause-and-effect progression, typical of a **diatribe**, showing that God’s judgment is a direct, logical **recompense** for human rebellion.

--- Part I: The Premise and Rejection (The Cause)
kicker: Romans 1:18-32
step: IF | God’s truth is clearly seen from creation, and wrath is revealed against ungodliness,
step: THEN | they are **without excuse**, *Because* they knew God.
step: BUT | they rejected this knowledge: they glorified him not as God, neither were thankful.
step: RESULT | They became vain in their imaginations, their foolish heart was darkened, and they **changed the glory** of God into idols.
step: THE ULTIMATE REJECTION | They changed the truth of God into a lie, and worshipped and served the **creature more than the Creator**.

--- Part II: The Sequence of Judgment (The Effect)
kicker: Romans 1:18-32
lead: For this rebellion, God delivers them to the natural and just consequences of their perversion (three “gave them up” judgments).
table: Judgment (Logical Marker) | God’s Action (“Gave Them Up”)
tr: **1st Judgment** (*Wherefore*) | God gave them up to **uncleanness** through the lusts of their own hearts.
tr: **2nd Judgment** (*For this cause*) | God gave them up unto **vile affections**.
tr: **3rd Judgment** (*And even as*) | God gave them over to a **reprobate mind**, to do those things which are not convenient.

--- Part II: The Resulting Sin (Recompense of Error)
kicker: Romans 1:18-32
step: 1st | To dishonour their own bodies between themselves.
step: 2nd | Women and men changing the natural use into that which is against nature (Lesbianism/Homosexuality), receiving the fitting **recompense of their error**.
step: 3rd | Being filled with all unrighteousness, even though they **know the judgment of God** (that they are worthy of death), they take pleasure in them that do them.

=== Review: Weeks 1 & 2
--- Romans Chapter 1 Review [title]
overline: Weeks 1 & 2 Summary
heading: ROMANS CHAPTER 1 REVIEW
sub: Weeks 1 & 2 Summary
image: lessons/romans/romans-1-too-late-reprobate.jpg | Too Late Reprobate - Lev 20:13 / Rom 1:28 | Too Late Reprobate: Lev. 20:13, Rom. 1:28

--- Author: Paul
- **Formerly Saul of Tarsus**, zealous Pharisee who persecuted the church
- Radically converted on the road to Damascus

--- The Church at Rome
- The **only major church** Paul wrote to that he did **not** personally plant
- Mixed congregation: believing Jews + former Roman pagans
- Already **famous throughout the world** for their faith ([[Romans 1:8]])

--- Major Themes of Romans
- Salvation is **by grace through faith alone**
- Gentile believers are **full and equal members** of God’s people
- Practical implications of the gospel in daily life

--- Literary Style: Diatribe
lead: A persuasive logical argument using if/then statements, hypothetical objections (interlocutor), and conversational tone.

--- Romans 1:1-17: Greeting & Theme
kicker: Review
big: Romans 1:16-17 | mark: not ashamed; power of God unto salvation; righteousness of God revealed from faith to faith

--- Romans 1:18-32: The Wrath of God Revealed
kicker: Review
- **God’s wrath** is presently revealed from heaven against all ungodliness
- Men are **without excuse**: God’s eternal power and divine nature clearly seen
- They **suppressed the truth** and refused to retain God in their knowledge
- Therefore God **gave them up / gave them over** (3 times) to a **reprobate mind**

--- The Downward Spiral
kicker: Review
- Exchanged worship of Creator → worship of created things (idolatry)
- Exchanged natural relations → homosexual practice (both women and men)
- Filled with all unrighteousness, resulting in this catalog of sin:

--- The Catalog of Sin
kicker: Review
- fornication
- wickedness
- covetousness
- maliciousness
- envy
- murder
- debate / strife
- deceit
- malignity
- whisperers / gossipers
- backbiters
- haters of God

--- The Catalog of Sin (continued)
kicker: Review
- despiteful / insolent
- proud
- boasters
- inventors of evil things
- disobedient to parents
- without understanding
- covenant-breakers
- without natural affection
- implacable
- unmerciful
- approving of those who practice these things

--- Knowing the Judgment of God
kicker: Review
big: Romans 1:32 | mark: knowing the judgment of God; have pleasure in them that do them
